    234  5e1e							; ------------------------------------------------------------ One Key Play
    235  5e1e							; CRSR DOWN or CRSR RIGHT (A = 1 / 2: which) pressed, ONE KEY PLAY on: the
    236  5e1e							; phrase's next step sounds. PENTATONIC PAIRS: two notes of the key's
    237  5e1e							; pentatonic scale, one apart (a third or a fourth), across the overlay's two
    238  5e1e							; octaves. CHORD NOTES: one note of the chord (the keys held or latched),
    239  5e1e							; over two octaves. EACH PRESS CUTS the last step or lets it RING ON (until
    240  5e1e							; the next). The notes sound while either key is down (latch: until the next
    241  5e1e							; press).
    242  5e1e				   OkpPress
    243  5e1e					      subroutine
    244  5e1e		       0d 79 c8 	      ora	okpDown
    245  5e21		       8d 79 c8 	      sta	okpDown
    246  5e24		       ad 76 c8 	      lda	okpRing	; RINGS ON: the last step stays
    247  5e27		       f0 15		      beq	.cut
    248  5e29		       ad 7a c8 	      lda	okpCount
    249  5e2c		       f0 10		      beq	.cut
    250  5e2e		       ad 7b c8 	      lda	okpNotes
    251  5e31		       8d 7d c8 	      sta	okpNotes+2
    252  5e34		       ad 7c c8 	      lda	okpNotes+1
